                                "sense_id": "a8c9cf80-6b5f-3493-9bac-1a4dbb1d19e6",
                                "text": "“This is the idea of catabolic collapse: that what we’re living through is a series of crises, sometimes followed by momentary resolution, but the long-term trend is downturn. It’s not going to be a sudden event that’s everything in a single day, which I think people like preppers are more accustomed to thinking.”"
